From: nix-config integration <noreply@local>
Subject: [PATCH] agentmemory: disable iii OpenTelemetry exporters

The managed runtime keeps its normal local logs, but does not need the
iii-engine OpenTelemetry observability worker or the Node SDK exporters.

--- a/iii-config.yaml
+++ b/iii-config.yaml
@@ -38,8 +38,8 @@
   - name: iii-observability
     config:
-      enabled: true
+      enabled: false
       service_name: agentmemory
       exporter: memory
       # 0.1 instead of 1.0: at full sampling under sustained load the
       # log subscriber falls behind, the worker emits a "Log trigger
       # subscriber lagged" WARN, and that WARN re-enters the same
@@ -49,6 +49,6 @@
       sampling_ratio: 0.1
-      metrics_enabled: true
-      logs_enabled: true
+      metrics_enabled: false
+      logs_enabled: false
       # Console output is off by default; the feedback path needs the
       # console layer to amplify. Re-enable per-session via env if you
       # need verbose tracing for debugging.
